      "title": "Competition #EDUC 50-238-26 Teaching Mathematics in Elementary School 2 (Winter 2027)",
      "description": "Competition #EDUC 50-238-26 Teaching Mathematics in Elementary School 2 (Winter 2027) | careerbeacon.com Competition #EDUC 50-238-26 Teaching Mathematics in Elementary School 2 (Winter 2027) Faculty of Professional Studies | Wolfville, Nova Scotia, Canada View job description Application Review How would you like to start? Select one of our quick apply options. Import Resume Previous Application Apply Manually Loading... Contact Information Cover Letter Choose an option below. Both choices are valued equally. Write Cover Letter Attach Cover Letter Cover Letter Options Resume/CV Attach Resume/CV Attachments (Optional) Attach documents that support your application (i.e., transcript or portfolio work) Upload Document Save and Continue Assistant Welcome to your job application! Remember always to put your best foot forward. Be as thorough as possible in the information you provide. Need clarification on something? Just check out the tips I offer you along the way. Tips Contact Information Education Work Experience Languages Core Skills Additional Skills Online Presence Highlights Cover Letter Resume/CV Contact Information I admit this is pretty self-explanatory. But, I do want to remind you to double check your phone number and email address. A tiny mistake could have big implications! Return to tips Education This is where you add all relevant education experience you wish to share. In the description, be sure to add what courses you excelled in and what projects you completed which were really cool. Return to tips Work Experience It’s necessary to share work experience related to the job you are applying for. In the description, be sure to highlight what your major accomplishments were in each previous role. This gives the employer insight into what your responsibilities were and what you are capable of. Use this section to detail any relevant volunteer experience as well. Return to tips Languages Pretty simple. Just select the languages in which you have a working proficiency. Easy peasy. Return to tips Core Skills Mindfully select the skills that help you perform at your best. Core skills are a way for employers to understand you so they can make informed decisions. So be honest ;) Return to tips Additional Skills Have more skills to share? Do it here! Return to tips Online Presence Perhaps you have a stellar blog or a great LinkedIn profile. Share the links here for the employer to explore. Return to tips Highlights The Highlights section appears at the very top of your application. It’s pretty important, so make it count! Highlight key achievements, mention things that stand out about you as a person and your experiences, and if you can, give them a bit of insight into your personality. Help them remember you. You’re amazing, so tell them. Return to tips Cover Letter If you choose Write Cover Letter, you can write it right here in the application. Or you can attach your cover letter (PDF recommended). Return to tips Resume/CV Here you can attach your resume. Attaching your resume here will not overwrite any other info you’ve already imported. We recommend you upload your resume as a PDF file. File types: .pdf,.docx,.doc,.rtf,.txt,.odt Maximum file size is 20 MB. Return to tips Attachments Some employers want to see more. Be sure to check the application to see if they request any additional documentation. Maximum file size is 20 MB. Return to tips Sorry, but it looks like you've missed something. Return to tips Need more help? Uploading file, please wait... Cancel upload × Error: The resume uploaded couldn't be imported properly. Our system only accepts certain file types (.doc, .docx, .pdf for example). If you can convert your file to one of these file types, we should be able to import all of your information. If you experience any issues, you can email us at [email protected] . Close Window Log in to your Alongside Account Wrong Username/Email and password combination. Sorry, but it looks like you'v